<section class="ph"><div class="ph-media"><img class="ph-img" src="/assets/img/photos/city-dearborn.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/city-dearborn-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/city-dearborn.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="800" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap ph-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><a href="/mi-cities-served/">Cities</a><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><span aria-current="page">Dearborn</span></nav><p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Metro Detroit · Wayne County</p><h1>Insurance Appraiser in Dearborn, Michigan</h1><p class="ph-lede">Dearborn is a city of sturdy brick homes, tidy lots and full basements, many built in the decades when Ford’s Rouge complex drew workers from around the world. Those basements have made flooding the city’s signature claim.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-maize" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-glass" href="/request-claim-review/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="ph-facts"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>Wayne County</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>Metro Detroit</dd></div><div><dt>Inspections</dt><dd>On site</dd></div></dl></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose">
<div class="local"><div><p class="local-k">Neighborhoods &amp; areas</p><p>east Dearborn, west Dearborn, Fairlane, Ford Homes Historic District, Springwells Park</p></div><div><p class="local-k">Housing mix</p><p>Dearborn is mostly 1920s–1950s brick bungalows, colonials and Tudors on modest lots, nearly all with full basements, plus larger homes and condos near Fairlane.</p></div><div><p class="local-k">Common claim drivers</p><ul class="chips"><li>Basement flooding</li><li>Sewer backup</li><li>Wind and hail</li><li>Fallen trees</li><li>Frozen pipes</li></ul></div></div>
<h2>Basement Floods and Storm Claims in Dearborn</h2>
<p>Few Michigan cities have been hit by basement flooding as often as Dearborn. Much of the city is served by older combined sewers, and its brick homes almost all have finished or partly finished basements. When a heavy storm overloads the system, water comes up through floor drains, and the result is ruined carpet, drywall, furnaces, water heaters and stored belongings.</p>
<h3>2014 and 2021: the floods that shaped local claims</h3>
<p>The August 11, 2014 storm flooded freeways and basements across metro Detroit, and Dearborn was among the hard-hit communities. In late June 2021, it happened again. Heavy rain closed stretches of I-94 and nearby freeways, and thousands of basements in Dearborn, Dearborn Heights and Detroit filled with water and sewage. Many homeowners discovered afterward that their backup coverage carried a low limit, or wasn’t on the policy at all.</p>
<h3>Where backup claims go wrong</h3>
<p>Even when sewer backup coverage applies, disputes about the amount are common. Estimates may leave out proper water extraction and drying, antimicrobial treatment for contaminated water, removal of drywall to a safe height, or replacement of mechanical equipment. Contents in a finished basement, such as furniture, electronics and family items, are often undervalued. We review the estimate and the moisture documentation, and we build a supported scope when the insurer’s falls short. Learn more on our <a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/water-sewer-backup-appraisal/">water and sewer backup appraisal</a> page.</p>
<h3>Brick homes and storm damage</h3>
<p>Brick bungalows and colonials in east and west Dearborn handle wind well, but their roofs, gutters and chimneys don’t always fare as well. The August 24, 2023 storms that brought several tornadoes to southeast Michigan and the February 2023 ice storm both left limbs on roofs across the area. In the Ford Homes Historic District and other older sections, slate, tile and original wood details can make repair costs higher than a standard estimate assumes.</p>
<p>Dearborn’s finished basements often hold far more than storage. Family rooms, bedrooms, laundry areas and mechanical rooms all sit below grade, so a backup can damage flooring, cabinetry, appliances and personal items at once. A complete room-by-room inventory and photos taken before cleanup give an appraiser solid ground to work from when the numbers are far apart.</p>
<div class="note"><b class="h">Check your backup limit</b>Many Michigan policies cover sewer and drain backup only through an endorsement with its own limit. Find that number on your declarations page before you dispute the amount.</div>
<p>Our guide to <a href="/great-lakes-claim-guides/basement-backup-coverage-gaps/">basement backup coverage gaps</a> explains how these endorsements typically work, and the <a href="/mi-claim-calculators/claim-gap-fee-estimator/">claim gap and fee estimator</a> can help you decide whether appraisal makes financial sense.</p>
<h2>Services available in Dearborn</h2>
<p>Every Michigan Insurance Appraiser service is available to owners in Dearborn and surrounding communities, including:</p>
<ul><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/appraisal-demand-representation/">Appraisal Demand Representation</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/homeowner-claim-appraiser/">Homeowner Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/commercial-condo-hoa-appraisal/">Commercial, Condo &amp; HOA Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/hail-roof-damage-appraisal/">Hail &amp; Roof Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/windstorm-tornado-appraisal/">Windstorm &amp; Tornado Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/ice-dam-frozen-pipe-appraisal/">Ice Dam &amp; Frozen Pipe Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/water-sewer-backup-appraisal/">Water &amp; Sewer Backup Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/fire-smoke-loss-appraisal/">Fire &amp; Smoke Loss Appraisal</a></li></ul>
<h2>Questions from Dearborn property owners</h2><div class="qa"><details><summary><span>Is basement flooding in Dearborn covered?</span><i class="qa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa-a"><p>It depends on the cause and your policy. Sewer or drain backup is often covered only by an endorsement with a set limit, while surface flooding is usually excluded and needs separate flood insurance. Read your declarations page and policy carefully.</p></div></details><details><summary><span>Can appraisal raise my sewer backup payment above the endorsement limit?</span><i class="qa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa-a"><p>No. Appraisal decides the amount of loss, but the policy limit still caps what the insurer owes. Appraisal is most useful when the insurer’s estimate is below the limit.</p></div></details></div>
